meta {
  name: Refresh
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "refreshToken": "{{businessRefreshToken}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data) {
    if (data.accessToken) bru.setEnvVar("businessAccessToken", data.accessToken);
    if (data.refreshToken) bru.setEnvVar("businessRefreshToken", data.refreshToken);
  }
}

docs {
  Exchange a refresh token for a new access + refresh pair (single-use
  rotation). Re-captures both tokens.

  The session is re-validated on every refresh (the access token itself is
  self-contained, so this is where admin changes take effect):
  - person inactive, or tenant membership INACTIVE → 403 ACCOUNT_INACTIVE;
  - the stored (branch + role) context is kept only while that assignment is
    still live — active, not revoked, per-branch status ACTIVE, branch not
    soft-deleted. Otherwise the new tokens land on the user's DEFAULT profile,
    exactly like a fresh login.
  - `profiles[]` in the new JWT omits assignments on soft-deleted branches.
}
